When a call spread its arguments, the VM moved them into a temporary array
that the garbage collector did not see. A tostring method that ran gc()
while the error for a spread value that is not an array was formatted freed
the array, and the error path leaked a reference to that spread value.

-- Testcase --
{%
	let o = proto({}, { tostring: function() { gc(); return "custom"; } });

	try {
		print(...[ {} ], ...o);
	}
	catch (e) {
		print(e.message, "\n");
	}

	try {
		print(.../x/);
	}
	catch (e) {
		print(e.message, "\n");
	}
%}
-- End --

-- Expect stdout --
(custom) is not iterable
(/x/) is not iterable
-- End --
